with their kid and never leave.

11:17.827 --> 11:20.557
Not that I don't love having you here.

11:20.730 --> 11:22.721
You're a delight.

11:23.799 --> 11:26.393
- I'm fine with the baby.
- Really?

11:26.569 --> 11:28.230
I'm kind of looking forward to it.

11:29.038 --> 11:30.972
Well, that's a novel approach.

11:31.140 --> 11:35.076
So if it's not the baby, then why have you
been such a dillweed lately?

11:35.244 --> 11:37.474
- None of your business.
- So it's a girl.

11:37.646 --> 11:39.978
- Just get out of my room.
- Make me.

11:40.149 --> 11:43.050
God, you're such a child.

11:45.354 --> 11:48.016
Oh, yeah, it's a girl.

11:48.657 --> 11:51.353
- Hmm. Jolene.
- Yeah.

11:51.527 --> 11:54.121
Jolene Melnick.

11:54.330 --> 11:57.925
- Nope, I don't think so.
- Why not? You could call her Jo or Josie.

11:58.100 --> 12:00.534
Kind of wanted to name her
after my grandma Mildred.

12:01.070 --> 12:05.097
- Mildred Melnick?
- Yeah. We could call her Mil or Millie.

12:05.274 --> 12:06.298
I'm sorry, Herb.

12:06.475 --> 12:10.502
With a name like Mildred you might as well
call her Staff Sergeant Melnick.

12:10.980 --> 12:13.574
- Herb, can you get the cookies for me?
- Oh, sure.

12:13.749 --> 12:17.116
We, uh, keep them on the top shelf
of the pantry. You know, Jake.

12:17.286 --> 12:20.619
Yeah. Charlie keeps his fudge nuggets
in the trunk of his car.

12:20.790 --> 12:22.815
Thank you, dear.

12:24.226 --> 12:26.160
What are you doing here?

12:26.862 --> 12:28.762
I'm helping my friend. Helping you.

12:28.931 --> 12:32.628
If not for me, our little girl would be
surrounded by metaphorical pony peni.

12:33.202 --> 12:36.831
Our little girl? I don't know what you
imagine happened between you and me...

12:37.006 --> 12:40.066
